---
/**
 * VentilationPerfusionMatch — "Alveolar gas calculator". The lesson's worked problem as a
 * calculator: arterial PCO2 from alveolar ventilation (PaCO2 = 0.863 x VCO2 / VA), alveolar PO2
 * from the simplified alveolar gas equation (PAO2 = FiO2 x (PB - PH2O) - PaCO2 / R), and the
 * alveolar-arterial difference as PAO2 minus a typed-in PaO2. Bars for PAO2, PaO2 and PaCO2 on
 * one pressure axis. Self-contained vanilla-TS Astro island. Original.
 */
---

<figure class="vpm card" data-vpm>
  <figcaption class="vpm-head">Alveolar gas calculator<span class="vpm-chip">⚙ original · interactive</span></figcaption>

  <svg class="vpm-svg" viewBox="0 0 340 206" role="img" data-svg aria-label="A bar chart of partial pressures in millimetres of mercury: calculated alveolar oxygen, arterial oxygen set by the learner with the alveolar-arterial difference shaded between the two bar ends, and arterial carbon dioxide.">
    <text x="14" y="20" font-size="10" font-weight="700" fill="#4b4b55" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="3" paint-order="stroke" data-t="a">Alveolar PO₂ (calculated) = 99.7 mmHg</text>
    <rect x="14" y="25" width="10" height="14" fill="#0e7c86" stroke="#4b4b55" stroke-width="1" data-bar-a></rect>

    <line x1="14" y1="25" x2="14" y2="79" stroke="#4b4b55" stroke-width="1" stroke-dasharray="1.5 2.5" data-guide></line>

    <text x="14" y="60" font-size="10" font-weight="700" fill="#4b4b55" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="3" paint-order="stroke" data-t="b">Arterial PO₂ (your value) = 92 mmHg</text>
    <rect x="14" y="65" width="10" height="14" fill="#8cc3c8" stroke="#4b4b55" stroke-width="1" data-bar-pa></rect>
    <rect x="14" y="65" width="10" height="14" fill="#e57200" fill-opacity="0.55" stroke="#e57200" stroke-width="1" data-bar-aa></rect>
    <line x1="14" y1="62" x2="14" y2="82" stroke="#1f1f27" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-dasharray="3 2" data-ref></line>

    <text x="14" y="100" font-size="10" font-weight="700" fill="#4b4b55" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="3" paint-order="stroke" data-t="c">Arterial PCO₂ (calculated) = 40 mmHg</text>
    <rect x="14" y="105" width="10" height="14" fill="#6c7a9c" stroke="#4b4b55" stroke-width="1" data-bar-c></rect>

    <line x1="14" y1="130" x2="326" y2="130" stroke="#4b4b55" stroke-width="1"></line>
    <g data-ticks></g>
    <text x="170" y="157" text-anchor="middle" font-size="9" fill="#4b4b55">partial pressure (mmHg)</text>

    <rect x="14" y="168" width="10" height="10" fill="#e57200" fill-opacity="0.55" stroke="#e57200" stroke-width="1"></rect>
    <text x="30" y="177" font-size="9" fill="#4b4b55" data-t="l1">A-a difference = 99.7 − 92 = 7.7 mmHg</text>
    <line x1="14" y1="189" x2="24" y2="189" stroke="#1f1f27" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-dasharray="3 2"></line>
    <text x="30" y="192" font-size="9" fill="#4b4b55" data-t="l2">dashed mark: PaO₂ if the difference stayed 7.7 mmHg</text>
  </svg>

  <div class="vpm-controls">
    <label class="vpm-slabel"><span>Alveolar ventilation VA <em data-out="va">4.2</em> L per min <small>(4.2 in the lesson’s worked problem; range made up)</small></span>
      <input type="range" data-in="va" min="1" max="8" step="0.1" value="4.2" />
    </label>
    <label class="vpm-slabel"><span>Inspired O₂ fraction FiO₂ <em data-out="fio2">0.21</em> <small>(0.21 is air; the lesson works 0.30 in step 7; range made up)</small></span>
      <input type="range" data-in="fio2" min="0.21" max="0.3" step="0.01" value="0.21" />
    </label>
    <label class="vpm-slabel"><span>Respiratory quotient R <em data-out="r">0.80</em> <small>(about 0.8 at steady state on a mixed diet; range made up)</small></span>
      <input type="range" data-in="r" min="0.7" max="1" step="0.01" value="0.8" />
    </label>
    <label class="vpm-slabel"><span>Measured arterial PO₂ PaO₂ <em data-out="pao2">92</em> mmHg <small>(92 in the worked problem; range made up)</small></span>
      <input type="range" data-in="pao2" min="40" max="150" step="1" value="92" />
    </label>
  </div>

  <dl class="vpm-readout">
    <div><dt>Arterial PCO₂, 0.863 × VCO₂ ÷ VA</dt><dd data-r="pco2">0.863 × 195 ÷ 4.2 = 40 mmHg</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Inspired PO₂ once humidified, FiO₂ × (PB − 47)</dt><dd data-r="pio2">0.21 × 713 = 149.7 mmHg</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Alveolar PO₂, inspired − PaCO₂ ÷ R</dt><dd data-r="pao2">149.7 − 50.0 = 99.7 mmHg</dd></div>
    <div><dt>A-a difference, PAO₂ − PaO₂</dt><dd data-r="aa">99.7 − 92 = 7.7 mmHg</dd></div>
    <div class="vpm-wide"><dt data-ref-label>PaO₂ that would keep the difference at the worked problem’s 7.7 mmHg (lesson step 7)</dt><dd data-r="ref">92.0 mmHg</dd></div>
  </dl>
  <p class="vpm-cap">In a young adult the A-a difference is under about 10 mmHg and it rises with age; it is a difference, not a diffusion gradient.</p>

  <p class="vpm-why" data-why role="status"></p>

  <p class="vpm-assume"><strong>In this sketch:</strong> steady state, near room air, at sea level; no shunt, no ventilation-perfusion spread, no diffusion limitation and no oxygen dissociation curve are modelled. Arterial PCO₂ stands in for alveolar PCO₂, as the lesson’s equation assumes, and is rounded to a whole mmHg as the worked problem does. Held fixed and illustrative: carbon dioxide output VCO₂ 195 mL per min (the worked problem’s made-up value for a healthy young adult at rest, supine), barometric pressure 760 mmHg, water vapour pressure 47 mmHg at 37 °C. R is assumed rather than measured, and is set here by hand independently of VCO₂. The slider ranges, including FiO₂ from 0.21 to 0.30, R from 0.70 to 1.00 and PaO₂ from 40 to 150 mmHg, are made up for the sketch. VA is set by hand; the sketch does not model the controller that, the lesson says, defends arterial PCO₂. PaO₂ is typed in, not calculated. The simplified equation omits a small correction that grows with PaCO₂ and with FiO₂, so treat values as good to a few mmHg.</p>

  <p class="vpm-foot">Alveolar PO₂ is calculated from what is breathed in, FiO₂ × (PB − 47), less the carbon dioxide term PaCO₂ ÷ R, and PaCO₂ falls as alveolar ventilation rises; the A-a difference is that calculated value minus the arterial PO₂ from a blood sample.</p>
</figure>

<script>
  const NS = 'http://www.w3.org/2000/svg';
  const INK = '#4b4b55';
  const VCO2 = 195;        // mL per min, lesson step 4 (made-up healthy young adult at rest, supine)
  const PB = 760;          // mmHg, lesson
  const PH2O = 47;         // mmHg at 37 C, lesson
  const K = 0.863;         // lesson's conversion constant
  const AA_REF = 7.7;      // mmHg, lesson steps 6 and 7
  const AX_MAX = 200;
  const X0 = 14, X1 = 326;
  const xs = (v: number) => X0 + (Math.max(0, Math.min(AX_MAX, v)) / AX_MAX) * (X1 - X0);
  const MINUS = '−';

  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-vpm]').forEach((root) => {
    const inp = (k: string) => root.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>('[data-in="' + k + '"]');
    const out = (k: string) => root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-out="' + k + '"]');
    const rd = (k: string) => root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-r="' + k + '"]');
    const tx = (k: string) => root.querySelector<SVGTextElement>('[data-t="' + k + '"]');
    const rc = (k: string) => root.querySelector<SVGRectElement>('[' + k + ']');
    const vaIn = inp('va'), fiIn = inp('fio2'), rIn = inp('r'), paIn = inp('pao2');
    const vaOut = out('va'), fiOut = out('fio2'), rOut = out('r'), paOut = out('pao2');
    const rPco2 = rd('pco2'), rPio2 = rd('pio2'), rPao2 = rd('pao2'), rAa = rd('aa'), rRef = rd('ref');
    const tA = tx('a'), tB = tx('b'), tC = tx('c'), tL1 = tx('l1'), tL2 = tx('l2');
    const barA = rc('data-bar-a'), barPa = rc('data-bar-pa'), barAa = rc('data-bar-aa'), barC = rc('data-bar-c');
    const refLine = root.querySelector<SVGLineElement>('[data-ref]');
    const guide = root.querySelector<SVGLineElement>('[data-guide]');
    const svg = root.querySelector<SVGSVGElement>('[data-svg]');
    const refLabel = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-ref-label]');
    const ticks = root.querySelector<SVGGElement>('[data-ticks]');
    const why = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-why]');
    if (!vaIn || !fiIn || !rIn || !paIn || !vaOut || !fiOut || !rOut || !paOut ||
        !rPco2 || !rPio2 || !rPao2 || !rAa || !rRef || !tA || !tB || !tC || !tL1 || !tL2 ||
        !barA || !barPa || !barAa || !barC || !refLine || !guide || !svg || !refLabel || !ticks || !why) return;

    for (let v = 0; v <= AX_MAX; v += 50) {
      const x = xs(v);
      const ln = document.createElementNS(NS, 'line');
      ln.setAttribute('x1', String(x)); ln.setAttribute('x2', String(x));
      ln.setAttribute('y1', '130'); ln.setAttribute('y2', '134');
      ln.setAttribute('stroke', INK); ln.setAttribute('stroke-width', '1');
      ticks.appendChild(ln);
      const t = document.createElementNS(NS, 'text');
      t.setAttribute('x', String(x)); t.setAttribute('y', '143');
      t.setAttribute('text-anchor', v === 0 ? 'start' : v === AX_MAX ? 'end' : 'middle');
      t.setAttribute('font-size', '9'); t.setAttribute('fill', INK);
      t.textContent = String(v);
      ticks.appendChild(t);
    }

    const sg = (n: number, d: number) => {
      const s = n.toFixed(d);
      return s.charAt(0) === '-' ? MINUS + s.slice(1) : s;
    };
    const f1 = (n: number) => sg(n, 1);

    function render() {
      const va = Math.round(parseFloat(vaIn!.value) * 10) / 10;
      const fio2 = Math.round(parseFloat(fiIn!.value) * 100) / 100;
      const r = Math.round(parseFloat(rIn!.value) * 100) / 100;
      const pa = parseInt(paIn!.value, 10);

      const pco2 = Math.round(K * VCO2 / va);          // rounded to a whole mmHg, as the worked problem does
      const pio2 = Math.round(fio2 * (PB - PH2O) * 10) / 10;   // rounded to 0.1 before subtracting, as shown
      const term = Math.round(pco2 / r * 10) / 10;
      const pao2 = Math.round((pio2 - term) * 10) / 10; // calculated alveolar PO2
      const below0 = pao2 <= 0;
      let aa = Math.round((pao2 - pa) * 10) / 10;
      if (Math.abs(aa) < 0.05) aa = 0;
      const aaR = Math.round(aa * 10) / 10;            // classify on the displayed value
      const refPa = pao2 - AA_REF;
      const termDiff = Math.round(((pco2 - 40) / r) * 10) / 10;                // change in the CO2 term relative to PaCO2 = 40

      vaOut!.textContent = va.toFixed(1);
      fiOut!.textContent = fio2.toFixed(2);
      rOut!.textContent = r.toFixed(2);
      paOut!.textContent = String(pa);

      rPco2!.textContent = '0.863 × ' + VCO2 + ' ÷ ' + va.toFixed(1) + ' = ' + pco2 + ' mmHg';
      rPio2!.textContent = fio2.toFixed(2) + ' × ' + (PB - PH2O) + ' = ' + f1(pio2) + ' mmHg';
      rPao2!.textContent = f1(pio2) + ' ' + MINUS + ' ' + f1(term) + ' = ' + f1(pao2) + ' mmHg';
      if (below0) {
        rAa!.textContent = 'not shown: the calculated alveolar PO₂ is below zero';
        rRef!.textContent = 'not shown: the calculated alveolar PO₂ is below zero';
      } else {
        rAa!.textContent = f1(pao2) + ' ' + MINUS + ' ' + pa + ' = ' + f1(aa) + ' mmHg';
        rRef!.textContent = refPa > 0 ? f1(refPa) + ' mmHg' : 'below zero (' + f1(refPa) + ' mmHg)';
      }

      refLabel!.textContent = 'PaO₂ that would keep the difference at the worked problem’s 7.7 mmHg' + (va === 2.1 ? ' (lesson step 7)' : '');

      // SVG text and bars
      tA!.textContent = below0
        ? 'Alveolar PO₂ (calculated) = ' + f1(pao2) + ' mmHg, below zero'
        : 'Alveolar PO₂ (calculated) = ' + f1(pao2) + ' mmHg';
      tB!.textContent = 'Arterial PO₂ (your value) = ' + pa + ' mmHg';
      tC!.textContent = 'Arterial PCO₂ (calculated) = ' + pco2 + ' mmHg';
      tL1!.textContent = below0
        ? 'A-a difference not shown (alveolar PO₂ below zero)'
        : 'A-a difference = ' + f1(pao2) + ' ' + MINUS + ' ' + pa + ' = ' + f1(aa) + ' mmHg';
      tL2!.textContent = below0 || refPa <= 0
        ? 'dashed mark: not drawn (PaO₂ would be below zero)'
        : 'dashed mark: PaO₂ if the difference stayed 7.7 mmHg';

      const xA = xs(Math.max(0, pao2)), xP = xs(pa), xC = xs(pco2);
      barA!.setAttribute('width', Math.max(0, xA - X0).toFixed(1));
      barPa!.setAttribute('width', Math.max(0, xP - X0).toFixed(1));
      barC!.setAttribute('width', Math.max(0, xC - X0).toFixed(1));
      if (below0) {
        barAa!.setAttribute('width', '0');
        guide!.style.display = 'none';
      } else {
        barAa!.setAttribute('x', Math.min(xA, xP).toFixed(1));
        barAa!.setAttribute('width', Math.abs(xA - xP).toFixed(1));
        guide!.style.display = '';
        guide!.setAttribute('x1', xA.toFixed(1));
        guide!.setAttribute('x2', xA.toFixed(1));
      }
      if (below0 || refPa <= 0) {
        refLine!.style.display = 'none';
      } else {
        refLine!.style.display = '';
        const xr = xs(refPa);
        refLine!.setAttribute('x1', xr.toFixed(1));
        refLine!.setAttribute('x2', xr.toFixed(1));
      }
      svg!.setAttribute('aria-label',
        'Partial pressures in millimetres of mercury: calculated alveolar oxygen ' + f1(pao2) +
        ', arterial oxygen ' + pa + ', arterial carbon dioxide ' + pco2 + '.');

      // status
      let s = 'In this sketch, alveolar ventilation of ' + va.toFixed(1) + ' L per min with a carbon dioxide output of ' + VCO2 +
        ' mL per min gives an arterial PCO₂ of ' + pco2 + ' mmHg, and inspired PO₂ of ' + f1(pio2) + ' mmHg less the carbon dioxide term ' +
        pco2 + ' ÷ ' + r.toFixed(2) + ' = ' + f1(term) + ' mmHg gives a calculated alveolar PO₂ of ' + f1(pao2) + ' mmHg.';

      if (pco2 < 40) {
        s += ' In this sketch, a PaCO₂ below 40 mmHg makes the carbon dioxide term ' + f1(-termDiff) + ' mmHg smaller than it would be at 40 mmHg with the same R, so the calculated alveolar PO₂ is that much higher.';
      } else if (pco2 > 40) {
        s += ' In this sketch, a PaCO₂ above 40 mmHg makes the carbon dioxide term ' + f1(termDiff) + ' mmHg larger than it would be at 40 mmHg with the same R, so the calculated alveolar PO₂ is that much lower.';
      }

      if (below0) {
        s += ' In this sketch, the equation returns a value below zero, which a partial pressure cannot be, so the A-a difference is not shown. The lesson also notes that the simplified equation omits a small correction that grows with PaCO₂ and with FiO₂.';
      } else if (aaR < 0) {
        s += ' In this sketch, the PaO₂ you set is ' + f1(-aa) + ' mmHg above the calculated alveolar PO₂, so the difference is ' + f1(aa) + ' mmHg. The lesson has arterial PO₂ below alveolar PO₂, and says R is assumed rather than measured, so this combination of values does not match the lesson’s account.';
      } else {
        s += ' In this sketch, the A-a difference is ' + f1(aa) + ' mmHg. The lesson gives under about 10 mmHg in a young adult, rising with age; the sketch has no age control.';
        if (aaR > 10) {
          s += ' The lesson lists ventilation-perfusion mismatch, shunt and diffusion limitation as mechanisms that widen the difference, and says hypoventilation leaves it normal; this sketch cannot tell which of the first three is at work.';
        } else if (pa < 92) {
          s += ' The lesson’s hypoventilation pattern is low PO₂, high PCO₂ and a normal difference; here PaCO₂ is ' + pco2 + ' mmHg and the difference is under about 10 mmHg.';
        }
      }

      if (fio2 > 0.21) {
        s += ' The lesson says the difference also rises with inspired oxygen fraction; this sketch keeps the PaO₂ you set and does not predict how the difference changes.';
      }

      const air = fio2 === 0.21 && r === 0.8;
      if (va === 4.2 && air) {
        s += pa === 92
          ? ' These are steps 3 to 6 of the lesson’s worked problem, whose values are made up for a healthy young adult at rest, supine, breathing air at sea level.'
          : ' These values match steps 3 to 5 of the lesson’s worked problem (made-up values for a healthy young adult at rest, supine, breathing air at sea level); its PaO₂ is 92 mmHg.';
      } else if (va === 2.1 && air) {
        s += ' This is the lesson’s step 7, halved alveolar ventilation at unchanged carbon dioxide output: PaCO₂ 80 mmHg and PAO₂ 49.7 mmHg. With the difference still 7.7 mmHg the lesson gets a PaO₂ of 42 mmHg.' +
          (pa === 42 ? ' You have set 42 mmHg.' : ' Set the PaO₂ slider to 42 to see it.');
      } else if (va === 2.1 && fio2 === 0.3 && r === 0.8) {
        s += ' This is the lesson’s step 7 at FiO₂ 0.30: PAO₂ 113.9 mmHg and, with the difference still 7.7 mmHg, a PaO₂ of about 106 mmHg, with PaCO₂ staying at 80 mmHg.';
      }
      why!.textContent = s;
    }

    [vaIn, fiIn, rIn, paIn].forEach((el) => {
      el.addEventListener('input', render);
      el.addEventListener('change', render);
    });
    render();
  });
</script>

<style>
  .vpm { padding: var(--ddp-space-3) var(--ddp-space-4) var(--ddp-space-4); margin: var(--ddp-space-5) 0; }
  .vpm-head { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: baseline; justify-content: space-between; gap: 0.3rem; font-weight: 600; font-size: var(--ddp-text-sm); color: var(--ddp-color-primary); margin-bottom: var(--ddp-space-3); }
  .vpm-chip { font-family: var(--ddp-font-mono); font-size: var(--ddp-text-xs); font-weight: 400; color: var(--ddp-color-muted); }
  .vpm-svg { display: block; width: 100%; max-width: 560px; margin: 0 auto; height: auto; background: #fff; border: 1px solid var(--ddp-color-line); border-radius: 6px; }
  .vpm-controls { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: var(--ddp-space-2) var(--ddp-space-4); margin: var(--ddp-space-3) 0 var(--ddp-space-2); }
  .vpm-slabel { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.1rem; font-size: var(--ddp-text-xs); color: var(--ddp-color-ink-soft); }
  .vpm-slabel small { font-size: inherit; color: var(--ddp-color-muted); }
  .vpm-slabel em { font-style: normal; font-weight: 700; color: var(--ddp-color-accent); font-family: var(--ddp-font-mono); }
  .vpm-slabel input { accent-color: var(--ddp-color-accent); }
  .vpm-readout { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: var(--ddp-space-2); margin: var(--ddp-space-2) 0; padding: var(--ddp-space-2) var(--ddp-space-3); background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--ddp-color-accent) 8%, transparent); border-radius: 6px; }
  .vpm-readout div { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.1rem; }
  .vpm-wide { grid-column: 1 / -1; }
  .vpm-readout dt { font-size: var(--ddp-text-xs); color: var(--ddp-color-muted); }
  .vpm-readout dd { margin: 0; font-family: var(--ddp-font-mono); font-size: var(--ddp-text-xs); color: var(--ddp-color-primary); font-weight: 700; }
  .vpm-cap { margin: 0 0 var(--ddp-space-2); font-size: var(--ddp-text-xs); color: var(--ddp-color-ink-soft); line-height: 1.45; }
  .vpm-why { margin: 0; font-size: var(--ddp-text-xs); color: var(--ddp-color-ink-soft); line-height: 1.5; min-height: 11em; }
  .vpm-assume { margin: var(--ddp-space-2) 0 0; font-size: var(--ddp-text-xs); color: var(--ddp-color-muted); line-height: 1.45; }
  .vpm-foot { margin: var(--ddp-space-3) 0 0; font-size: var(--ddp-text-xs); color: var(--ddp-color-ink-soft); border-left: 3px solid var(--ddp-color-secondary); padding-left: 0.55rem; }
  @media (max-width: 520px) {
    .vpm-controls { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .vpm-readout { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .vpm-why { min-height: 20em; }
  }
</style>
